===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A tool used for [[drilling]].
# {{lb|en|MLE|slang}} A [[knife]] [[fit]] for a [[stabbing]].
#: {{syn|en|wetter|jook|jooker|chete|ching|ying|rambo|poker|pokey|bassy|shank|nank|splash|splasher|cheffer|cutter}}
# A person who bores or drills; a person employed to drill bore holes.
# A [[tedious]] person, who bores others; a [[bore]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1896|author=Harry Persons Taber; Elbert Hubbard|journal=The Philistine|volume=3|page=21
|passage=The boree has been heard from frequently since the Renaissance, and his sentiments have undergone little change. The '''borer''' hasn't had much to say for himself.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Margaret Atwood|title=Bodily Harm
|passage=Rennie was an expert on boredom, having done a piece on it for Pandora's “Relationships” column in which she claimed that there were two people involved in boredom, not just one: the '''borer''' and the boree.}}
# An [[insect]] or insect [[larva]] that bores into wood.
# One of the many types of [[mollusc]] that bore into soft rock.
# A [[cyclostome]], such as a [[hagfish]], which bores into [[injured]], dead, or [[decaying]] sea creatures to feed on their flesh.

